# Local notes for this machine

Setup copies this file to `CLAUDE.local.md`, which git ignores and root reads when it is present. Replace each `<placeholder>`. Keep machine-specific facts here and never copy them into tracked files. Never write a token, password or key in this file.

## This machine

- Machine id and label, as in `registry.json`: `<machine id>` / `<machine label>`
- Operating system and shell: `<for example Windows 11, PowerShell 7>`
- Where project folders live: `<folder>`
- Anything root must know before it starts or stops sessions here: `<notes>`

## Claude homes

One row for each Claude login on this machine. The folder is what `CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR` points at.

| Name | Folder | Account | Used for |
|---|---|---|---|
| `<default>` | `<folder>` | `<account email or nickname>` | `<root, which projects>` |

## Codex accounts

One row for each entry of `codex_accounts` in `registry.json`. The folder is that account's Codex home.

| Alias | Folder | Account | Used for |
|---|---|---|---|
| `<alias>` | `<folder>` | `<account email or nickname>` | `<which projects>` |

## Discord bots

- This machine's root bot: `<bot name>`
- Root channel: `<channel name>`
- Category for this machine's projects: `<category name>`
- Another machine's root bot in the same server, if there is one: `<bot name>`

## Access exceptions

- `<project or channel>`: `<who may do what>`
